WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:05.460
Sal Vulcano is one quarter of The Tenderloins,
the comedy troupe at the heart of the truTV

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.780
show Impractical Jokers, which has been on
air since 2011.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.160
If you've somehow never seen it before, the
series follows Vulcano and his longtime friends

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:17.930
James Murray, Joe Gatto, and Brian Quinn as
they compete to be the last man standing in

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.840
public practical joke challenges.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.980
Examples include cutting in line in ludicrous
ways, soliciting for hilariously fake charities,

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.100
and even straight-up insulting strangers,
just to see what happens.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.480
"You just gotta say 'Howdy, ass----."

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.800
"Howdy, ass----."

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.000
"Oh!"

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.280
The results are always awkward, but the Joker
has to do it, the loser faces punishment,

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.120
and that's almost always worse.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.820
"This is ridiculous."

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.940
The gang's friendship must be pretty ironclad
for them to still be pals after regularly

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.140
tormenting each other over the course of a
decade.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.440
How did it all come together?

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.980
This time, let's focus on Sal Vulcano, and
see what he was doing before Impractical Jokers

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:57.480
took off.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.200
"Look out!

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.400
Look the f--- out!"

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:07.120
Born in 1976 in Staten Island, New York, Salvatore
"Sal" Vulcano is the only brother to three

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.750
sisters Kelly Ann, Diane, and Jenna, the last
of whom has actually appeared on Impractical

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.200
Jokers and even married Murray as a prank.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.220
"I, James Murray, take you, Sal's sister —"

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:25.400
Sal's parents, Sal Vulcano Sr. and Dianne
Fernandez-Vulcano, divorced when he was very

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:25.900
young.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.800
Between them, Vulcano has Italian, Cuban,
and Puerto Rican roots.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.210
Vulcano's fate as a comedian began to take
shape when he was a teenager in the 90s, when

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:37.140
he began attending the private Monsignor Farrell
High School.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.750
There, Vulcano participated in several sports,
was a member of the chess club, and in his

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.550
junior year joined the school's improv club,
where he met the other three men that would

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:48.100
in adulthood become his best friends and co
stars.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:52.280
Unlike the reputation they cultivate on screen,
Vulcano and the other boys are remembered

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.360
as being rather respectful young men in high
school, a fact they often bring up themselves

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.280
as a reason why they never perform pranks
too out-of-line.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:01:59.320
"Touch his groin!

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.200
Touch his groin!"

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:01.280
"Nah."

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:07.380
Between 2010 and 2014, Sal put his background
as a bartender and his finance degree from

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:12.560
St. John's University to use as business manager
for a bar called Full Cup, a well-known music

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.140
and comedy venue in his home borough that
had gone through several owners in its long

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:16.960
local history.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:21.440
After Impractical Jokers catapulted him into
the national spotlight, he sold his stake

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.580
in the bar in 2014, and sadly the business
soon struggled to survive.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.760
It was rebranded as the Hashtag Bar under
new management in 2016, and ultimately closed

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.460
later that year.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.920
Turns out, Sal was pretty important to keeping
the place afloat.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.920
As Sal's former business partner, Robert Parker,
told SI Live in 2016,

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.500
"My famous partner left me.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.240
Sal was the professional business guy, so
when he left, it was really hard."

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:48.560
Along with that work, Vulcano assisted friend
and fellow Staten Island local Jay Miller

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:52.620
with writing for his longtime local-access
comedy talk show Midevenings with Jay Miller,

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.970
a Staten Island entertainment institution
that gives local musicians and other talent

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.800
a platform, David Letterman-style.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.480
The two got on so well creatively that Sal
asked Jay to join Impractical Jokers as a

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.820
producer in 2013.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:08.240
"I just wanna say, you are number one in my
book."

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.760
Before landing the lucrative TV deal that
became Impractical Jokers, Sal and the others

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.020
toured and performed live shows as comedy
quartet The Tenderloins.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.140
They also self-produced sketch comedy content
for a number of years during the early days

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:20.820
of YouTube.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.980
The channel is still active, and many of their
oldest videos are available to watch if you've

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.380
got a free afternoon to dive into a decade's
worth of memories.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.000
"You do not do that!"

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.880
That sketch comedy work got them significant
attention, first in the form of a failed scripted

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:44.090
comedy pilot for SpikeTV, and then the television
deal with truTV for the series that eventually

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.620
became Impractical Jokers.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.660
With all their previous material available
online as a proof-of-concept, as well as their

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:53.900
professional background touring, they were
given unusually generous creative control

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.600
as executive producers for their first big
deal television foray.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.410
If the best improv is fostered through a sense
of trust, Vulcano and the Impractical Jokers

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.930
boys certainly have it, and that's all thanks
to time and experience.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.380
With trust comes the understanding that when
conflict comes, they can manage it between

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:08.880
each other.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.940
As Sal explained in a Reddit AMA,

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.080
"Of course we fight from time to time, but
we are so used to it, it's never personal."

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.970
"Ah, I love watching your blood boil."

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:18.880
"Oh, you f---in'..."

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:22.660
If that isn't an ultimate statement on the
strength of this foursome's friendship, we

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:23.480
aren't sure what is.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.990
It must have been fate for the four of them
to spend their lives doing this to each other,

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.100
and it couldn't be more charming to watch.

